# Secrets — .env.example is the tracked template
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Service-account keys and anything else with a private key in it. A committed
# GCS key is a full compromise of gs://btvaroska, which also holds this estate's
# .env backups. See docs/runbooks/artifact-storage.md.
secrets/
# The device simulator's NVS analogue (R0-test-1). Every file in here is a LIVE
# broker credential: `POST /v1/enroll` returns `mqtt_password` once and it exists
# nowhere else — not in Postgres, not in a log, not in dynsec (which keeps a hash).
# A committed .sim/ is a committed fleet credential. Files are written 0600.
.sim/
# The QEMU harness's working directory (R0-fw-1). Same posture as `.sim/`, and for
# a stronger reason: `.qemu/ff_cfg.bin` holds a LIVE single-use enrollment token, and
# `.qemu/flash-<target>.bin` holds the NVS the emulated board wrote its `mqtt_password`
# into after enrolling. A committed .qemu/ is a committed fleet credential inside a
# 4 MB binary nobody would think to grep. Created 0700 by `just agent-qemu`.
.qemu/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage

# Node / dashboard
node_modules/
dist/

# System
.DS_Store

# Agent plan files — local scratch, never shared
.claude/plans/

# Agent firmware (R0-infra-2).
# `sdkconfig` is generated by idf.py on the first build and WINS over
# sdkconfig.defaults from then on — a committed one would silently ship a bootloader
# whose rollback option no longer matches agent/sdkconfig.defaults. Builds happen in
# the container, where no stale copy exists.
agent/build/
agent/sdkconfig
agent/sdkconfig.old
# Bundles are build outputs (~1.2 MB per target), rebuilt with `just agent-build`.
# The directory itself is tracked so `COPY agent/dist` works on a clean clone.
# `!agent/dist/` has to come FIRST: the `dist/` rule in the Node section above matches
# any directory of that name at any depth, and git never descends into an excluded
# directory — so `!agent/dist/.gitkeep` alone would silently do nothing.
!agent/dist/
agent/dist/*
!agent/dist/.gitkeep
